<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Britannia Secunda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 300–5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Britannia Secunda was one of the provinces created in Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> by the reforms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diocletian">Diocletian</a> around 300. It covered northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eboracum">Eboracum</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a>). With the other British provinces it formed the Diocese of the Britains under a vicarius in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p></div>
